<body>
<header class="top"><div class="topin">
<a class="logo" href="#top">Aux</a>
<nav aria-label="Sections"><a href="#palette">Palette</a><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a><a href="#contrast">Text on color</a><a href="#type">Typography</a><a href="#space">Spacing &amp; shape</a><a href="#components">Components</a><a href="#writing">Voice</a><a href="#a11y">Accessibility</a></nav>
<button class="tg" id="tg" role="switch" aria-checked="false"><span class="trk"><span class="knob"></span></span>Dark mode</button>
</div></header>
<main id="top">
<div class="hero">
<div><h1>Aux</h1><p>The design reference for the Aux web app. Inspired by Last.fm: a white page, dark text, light gray panels, and one purple accent used sparingly. For Muaz, RJ and Milind. If a value isn't here, ask before inventing one.</p></div>
<svg viewBox="0 0 480 288" role="img" aria-label="Aux brand blocks">
<rect class="pu" x="16" y="-8" width="176" height="272" rx="6"/><rect class="ik" x="208" y="-8" width="128" height="64" rx="6"/><rect class="so" x="208" y="72" width="128" height="192" rx="6"/><rect class="gr" x="352" y="136" width="144" height="128" rx="6"/>
<rect class="bar" x="40" y="200" width="8" height="40" rx="3"/><rect class="bar" x="56" y="152" width="8" height="88" rx="3"/><rect class="bar" x="72" y="120" width="8" height="120" rx="3"/><rect class="bar" x="88" y="176" width="8" height="64" rx="3"/><rect class="bar" x="104" y="136" width="8" height="104" rx="3"/><rect class="bar" x="120" y="96" width="8" height="144" rx="3"/><rect class="bar" x="136" y="160" width="8" height="80" rx="3"/><rect class="bar" x="152" y="192" width="8" height="48" rx="3"/><rect class="bar" x="168" y="168" width="8" height="72" rx="3"/>
</svg>
</div>

<section id="palette">
<h2>The palette</h2>
<p class="lead">Two main colors, purple and white, plus neutrals. Purple plays the role Last.fm gives its red: primary buttons, the play button, chart bars, active tabs and links.</p>
<div class="pal"><div class="sw"><div class="chip" style="background:#6a4778"></div><div class="swb"><p class="swn">purple</p><p class="swh">#6A4778</p></div></div><div class="sw"><div class="chip" style="background:#ffffff"></div><div class="swb"><p class="swn">white</p><p class="swh">#FFFFFF</p></div></div><div class="sw"><div class="chip" style="background:#f5f5f5"></div><div class="swb"><p class="swn">surface-alt</p><p class="swh">#F5F5F5</p></div></div><div class="sw"><div class="chip" style="background:#222222"></div><div class="swb"><p class="swn">ink</p><p class="swh">#222222</p></div></div><div class="sw"><div class="chip" style="background:#6b6b6b"></div><div class="swb"><p class="swn">ink-muted</p><p class="swh">#6B6B6B</p></div></div><div class="sw"><div class="chip" style="background:#e5e5e5"></div><div class="swb"><p class="swn">line</p><p class="swh">#E5E5E5</p></div></div><div class="sw"><div class="chip" style="background:#f1ecf3"></div><div class="swb"><p class="swn">purple-soft</p><p class="swh">#F1ECF3</p></div></div><div class="sw"><div class="chip" style="background:#573a63"></div><div class="swb"><p class="swn">purple-hover</p><p class="swh">#573A63</p></div></div></div>
<div class="note">Keep it simple. Most of any screen is white with dark text; gray panels group things; purple appears in small, deliberate spots, usually one main button and a few accents per screen. If a screen looks purple, there's too much of it. Purple is never a full-page background. <code>danger</code> and <code>success</code> are for error and confirmation messages only.</div>
</section>

<section id="tokens">
<h2>Color tokens</h2>
<p class="lead">Write CSS against these role names, never raw hex, so the dark mode toggle works for free. A sidebar is <code>background: var(--surface-alt); color: var(--ink)</code>, not <code>#F5F5F5</code>.</p>
<div class="tw"><table><thead><tr><th>Token</th><th>Light</th><th>Dark</th><th>Usage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span class="dot" style="background:var(--purple)"></span><code>purple</code></td><td class="hx">#6A4778</td><td class="hx">#6A4778</td><td>The brand color, used the way Last.fm uses its red: primary buttons, the play button, active tab underline, chart bars, the match badge. Use it for accents, not large backgrounds. White text on it is 7.5:1.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="dot" style="background:var(--purple-hover)"></span><code>purple-hover</code></td><td class="hx">#573A63</td><td class="hx">#7D5A8C</td><td>Hover and pressed state for anything purple.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="dot" style="background:var(--purple-soft)"></span><code>purple-soft</code></td><td class="hx">#F1ECF3</td><td class="hx">#2A2030</td><td>Light purple tint: selected chips, the playing row, highlighted list items. Main text on it passes in both themes.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="dot" style="background:var(--white)"></span><code>white</code></td><td class="hx">#FFFFFF</td><td class="hx">#FFFFFF</td><td>The second main color. Page background in light mode and text on purple fills.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="dot" style="background:var(--surface)"></span><code>surface</code></td><td class="hx">#FFFFFF</td><td class="hx">#121212</td><td>Page background. Dark value is speculative (see Dark mode).</td></tr><tr><td><span class="dot" style="background:var(--surface-alt)"></span><code>surface-alt</code></td><td class="hx">#F5F5F5</td><td class="hx">#1E1E1E</td><td>Light gray panels: sidebars, the player bar, section backgrounds, hover rows.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="dot" style="background:var(--ink)"></span><code>ink</code></td><td class="hx">#222222</td><td class="hx">#F2F2F2</td><td>Main text and headings, on surface, surface-alt and purple-soft (13.7:1 or better).</td></tr><tr><td><span class="dot" style="background:var(--ink-muted)"></span><code>ink-muted</code></td><td class="hx">#6B6B6B</td><td class="hx">#A3A3A3</td><td>Secondary text: artist names, timestamps, play counts. Passes on surface and surface-alt in both themes (4.9:1 or better).</td></tr><tr><td><span class="dot" style="background:var(--line)"></span><code>line</code></td><td class="hx">#E5E5E5</td><td class="hx">#2E2E2E</td><td>Hairline dividers between rows and around cards. Decorative only.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="dot" style="background:var(--line-strong)"></span><code>line-strong</code></td><td class="hx">#8A8A8A</td><td class="hx">#6B6B6B</td><td>Input and checkbox borders, which need 3:1 to be visible as controls.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="dot" style="background:var(--primary)"></span><code>primary</code></td><td class="hx">#6A4778</td><td class="hx">#6A4778</td><td>Fill for primary buttons, the play button and the match badge. Same purple in both themes.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="dot" style="background:var(--on-primary)"></span><code>on-primary</code></td><td class="hx">#FFFFFF</td><td class="hx">#FFFFFF</td><td>Text and icons on a primary fill (7.5:1).</td></tr><tr><td><span class="dot" style="background:var(--link)"></span><code>link</code></td><td class="hx">#6A4778</td><td class="hx">#B593C4</td><td>Purple text: links, active tab labels, the playing song's title. Lighter in dark mode because the brand purple is too dark to read on black (2.5:1).</td></tr><tr><td><span class="dot" style="background:var(--focus-ring)"></span><code>focus-ring</code></td><td class="hx">#6A4778</td><td class="hx">#B593C4</td><td>2px keyboard focus outline with a 2px gap. Every clickable element gets it.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="dot" style="background:var(--danger)"></span><code>danger</code></td><td class="hx">#B42318</td><td class="hx">#F97066</td><td>Error messages only (failed upload, wrong password). Text on surface.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="dot" style="background:var(--success)"></span><code>success</code></td><td class="hx">#2E7D5B</td><td class="hx">#6CCB9A</td><td>Confirmation messages only (upload done, followed). Text on surface.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h3>Dark mode (speculative)</h3>
<p>Dark mode is a proposal, not a commitment. It swaps white for near-black (#121212) and gray panels for #1E1E1E, keeps purple buttons exactly as they are, and uses a lighter purple (#B593C4) for purple text and links, because the brand purple is too dark to read on black. The toggle sets <code>data-theme="light"</code> or <code>data-theme="dark"</code> on <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>, saves the choice in localStorage, and defaults to light. If the team drops dark mode, delete the toggle and nothing else changes. Try the switch at the top of this page.</p>
</section>

<section id="contrast">
<h2>Text on color</h2>
<p class="lead">Every approved pairing with its contrast ratio. Minimum is 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for 24px and up (or 18px bold).</p>
<div class="pairs">
<div class="pr" style="background:#fff;color:#222"><span class="t">Ink on white</span><span class="m">15.9 : 1 · all text</span></div>
<div class="pr" style="background:#f5f5f5;color:#222"><span class="t">Ink on gray</span><span class="m">14.6 : 1 · all text</span></div>
<div class="pr" style="background:#6a4778;color:#fff;border-color:#6a4778"><span class="t">White on purple</span><span class="m">7.5 : 1 · buttons, badges</span></div>
<div class="pr" style="background:#fff;color:#6a4778"><span class="t">Purple on white</span><span class="m">7.5 : 1 · links, accents</span></div>
<div class="pr" style="background:#f5f5f5;color:#6a4778"><span class="t">Purple on gray</span><span class="m">6.9 : 1 · links on panels</span></div>
<div class="pr" style="background:#f1ecf3;color:#222"><span class="t">Ink on purple tint</span><span class="m">13.7 : 1 · selected rows</span></div>
<div class="pr" style="background:#fff;color:#6b6b6b"><span class="t">Muted on white</span><span class="m">5.3 : 1 · secondary text</span></div>
<div class="pr" style="background:#f5f5f5;color:#6b6b6b"><span class="t">Muted on gray</span><span class="m">4.9 : 1 · secondary text</span></div>
<div class="pr" style="background:#121212;color:#b593c4;border-color:#333"><span class="t">Light purple on dark</span><span class="m">7.1 : 1 · dark mode links</span></div>
<div class="pr" style="background:#121212;color:#6a4778;border-color:#333"><span class="t no">Purple on dark</span><span class="m" style="color:#f2f2f2">2.5 : 1 · never for text</span></div>
</div>
</section>

<section id="type">
<h2>Typography</h2>
<p class="lead">One family: Montserrat from Google Fonts, falling back to Segoe UI and Helvetica. Nothing smaller than 12px. Headings use sentence case ("Your playlists", not "Your Playlists"). Avoid all caps except very short badge text.</p>
<div class="ty"><div class="tym"><code>display</code><span>40px / 44px · 800</span></div><p style="font-size:40px;line-height:44px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Find people who hear it too</p><p class="tyu">One per page at most: landing hero, empty-state headline.</p></div><div class="ty"><div class="tym"><code>heading-1</code><span>28px / 34px · 700</span></div><p style="font-size:28px;line-height:34px;font-weight:700;">Your playlists</p><p class="tyu">Page titles.</p></div><div class="ty"><div class="tym"><code>heading-2</code><span>20px / 28px · 700</span></div><p style="font-size:20px;line-height:28px;font-weight:700;">Top artists</p><p class="tyu">Section titles inside a page.</p></div><div class="ty"><div class="tym"><code>body</code><span>16px / 24px · 400</span></div><p style="font-size:16px;line-height:24px;font-weight:400;">Upload your MP3s and build playlists you actually own.</p><p class="tyu">Paragraphs, form fields, bios.</p></div><div class="ty"><div class="tym"><code>body-strong</code><span>16px / 24px · 600</span></div><p style="font-size:16px;line-height:24px;font-weight:600;">Midnight Drive</p><p class="tyu">Song titles, usernames, button labels.</p></div><div class="ty"><div class="tym"><code>small</code><span>14px / 20px · 500</span></div><p style="font-size:14px;line-height:20px;font-weight:500;">Frank Ocean · 3:42</p><p class="tyu">Artist names, play counts, metadata. Use ink-muted.</p></div><div class="ty"><div class="tym"><code>caption</code><span>12px / 16px · 600</span></div><p style="font-size:12px;line-height:16px;font-weight:600;">87% match</p><p class="tyu">Badges, chip labels, timestamps. Never smaller than 12px.</p></div>
</section>

<section id="space">
<h2>Spacing &amp; shape</h2>
<p class="lead">A 4px base. Cards get <code>space-4</code> padding; page sections are separated by <code>space-6</code>.</p>
<div class="spr"><code>space-1</code><span class="spb" style="width:4px"></span><span class="hx">4px</span><span class="spu">Icon to label gap.</span></div><div class="spr"><code>space-2</code><span class="spb" style="width:8px"></span><span class="hx">8px</span><span class="spu">Gap between chips and small items.</span></div><div class="spr"><code>space-3</code><span class="spb" style="width:12px"></span><span class="hx">12px</span><span class="spu">List row padding, gap inside cards.</span></div><div class="spr"><code>space-4</code><span class="spb" style="width:16px"></span><span class="hx">16px</span><span class="spu">Card padding, gap between list rows and cards.</span></div><div class="spr"><code>space-6</code><span class="spb" style="width:24px"></span><span class="hx">24px</span><span class="spu">Gap between page sections, page side margin on mobile.</span></div><div class="spr"><code>space-8</code><span class="spb" style="width:32px"></span><span class="hx">32px</span><span class="spu">Page side margin on desktop, space above page titles.</span></div>
<h3>Corners</h3>
<p>Small and crisp, like Last.fm. No drop shadows and no gradients: separate things with <code>surface-alt</code> backgrounds or a 1px <code>line</code> divider. Lists are flat rows split by hairlines, not stacks of cards.</p>
<div class="rds"><div class="rd"><div class="rdb" style="border-radius:3px"></div><code>radius-sm</code><span class="hx">3px</span><p class="spu">Buttons, inputs, album art thumbnails. Small and crisp, like Last.fm.</p></div><div class="rd"><div class="rdb" style="border-radius:6px"></div><code>radius-md</code><span class="hx">6px</span><p class="spu">Cards, the player bar, modals.</p></div><div class="rd"><div class="rdb" style="border-radius:999px"></div><code>radius-pill</code><span class="hx">999px</span><p class="spu">Genre chips, the match badge, the round play button and the theme toggle.</p></div></div>
</section>

<section id="components">
<h2>Components</h2>
<p class="lead">Live examples. Hover and tab through them; flip the dark mode switch to see both themes.</p>

<h3>Buttons</h3>
<div class="demo"><div class="row"><button class="btn primary">Upload song</button><button class="btn secondary">Create playlist</button><button class="btn text">See all</button><button class="btn primary" disabled>Follow</button></div></div>
<p class="rules">One primary button per view, labeled with a verb that says what happens. Primary: <code>primary</code> fill, <code>on-primary</code> text, <code>purple-hover</code> on hover. Secondary: <code>surface</code> fill, 1px <code>line-strong</code> border. Text button: <code>link</code> color, underline on hover, for "Cancel" or "See all". Disabled: 40% opacity. All: 10 × 18px padding, <code>radius-sm</code>, 2px <code>focus-ring</code> on keyboard focus.</p>

<h3>Track row</h3>
<div class="demo" style="padding:var(--space-2)">
<div class="tr"><span class="rk">1</span><button class="play" aria-label="Play Midnight Drive"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 14 14" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 1.5v11l9-5.5z" fill="currentColor"/></svg></button><div class="art"></div><div><p class="ti">Midnight Drive</p><p class="ar">Lena Park</p></div><div class="cnt"><div class="ctrk"><div class="fill" style="width:100%"></div></div><span class="ct">142 plays</span></div></div>
<div class="tr on"><span class="rk">2</span><button class="play" aria-label="Pause Glass Houses"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 14 14" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 1.5h3v11H3zM8 1.5h3v11H8z" fill="currentColor"/></svg></button><div class="art b"></div><div><p class="ti">Glass Houses</p><p class="ar">The Low Tides</p></div><div class="cnt"><div class="ctrk"><div class="fill" style="width:71%"></div></div><span class="ct">101 plays</span></div></div>
<div class="tr"><span class="rk">3</span><button class="play" aria-label="Play Slow Summer"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 14 14" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 1.5v11l9-5.5z" fill="currentColor"/></svg></button><div class="art c"></div><div><p class="ti">Slow Summer</p><p class="ar">Nadia Reyes</p></div><div class="cnt"><div class="ctrk"><div class="fill" style="width:44%"></div></div><span class="ct">63 plays</span></div></div>
</div>
<p class="rules">Flat Last.fm-style chart row: rank, play button, 40px album art (<code>radius-sm</code>), title in <code>body-strong</code>, artist and play count in <code>small</code> <code>ink-muted</code>. Rows split by 1px <code>line</code>. Hover turns a row <code>surface-alt</code>; the playing row gets <code>purple-soft</code>, a <code>link</code>-colored title and a filled play button. The play-count bar is <code>purple</code>, its length relative to the top song. No art? Show a <code>surface-alt</code> square with a music-note icon.</p>

<h3>Compatibility score</h3>
<div class="demo"><div class="card">
<div class="ctop"><div class="av" aria-hidden="true">J</div><p class="cs">Your musical compatibility with <b>jordan.k</b> is <span class="lv">Super</span></p></div>
<div class="meter" role="img" aria-label="87 percent compatible"><span class="seg f"></span><span class="seg f"></span><span class="seg f"></span><span class="seg f"></span><span class="seg f"></span><span class="pct">87%</span></div>
<p class="sh">You both listen to <a href="#components">Frank Ocean</a>, <a href="#components">SZA</a> and <a href="#components">Mitski</a>.</p>
</div></div>
<p class="rules">Modeled on Last.fm's musical compatibility meter. Five segments, filled ones <code>purple</code>. The level word is <code>link</code>-colored. Never color-code the score red, yellow or green; the word and meter carry the meaning. Levels:</p>
<div class="lvls"><span>0–19% Low</span><span>20–39% Medium</span><span>40–59% High</span><span>60–79% Very high</span><span>80–100% Super</span></div>

<h3>Theme toggle</h3>
<p class="rules" style="margin-top:0">The switch in this page's header. A real <code>&lt;button role="switch"&gt;</code> with <code>aria-checked</code>, a 40 × 22px <code>radius-pill</code> track: <code>surface-alt</code> when off, <code>primary</code> when on, white knob, labeled "Dark mode". Ships only if the team keeps dark mode.</p>
</section>

<section id="writing">
<h2>Voice</h2>
<p class="lead">Short, plain, friendly.</p>
<div class="dodont">
<div class="dd"><h4>Do</h4><ul><li>Buttons say exactly what happens: "Upload song", "Create playlist", "Follow".</li><li>Empty states say what to do next: "No songs yet. Upload an MP3 to start your library."</li><li>Errors say what went wrong and how to fix it: "That file isn't an MP3. Try another file."</li></ul></div>
<div class="dd x"><h4>Don't</h4><ul><li>Vague labels like "Submit" or "OK".</li><li>Apologetic or cute error messages.</li><li>Title Case headings or all caps.</li></ul></div>
</div>
</section>

<section id="a11y">
<h2>Accessibility &amp; icons</h2>
<p>Every clickable element shows a 2px <code>focus-ring</code> outline when reached by keyboard. Don't rely on color alone for state: a selected chip also gets a check icon, an error also gets text. Icon-only buttons need an accessible label. Text meets 4.5:1 contrast; control borders use <code>line-strong</code> to meet 3:1.</p>
<p>No logo exists yet, so the wordmark is "Aux" in Montserrat 800 in <code>purple</code>, top left of the header. Use one outline icon set throughout (Lucide is a good free choice) at 20px, stroke 2, in <code>ink</code> or <code>ink-muted</code>.</p>
</section>
</main>
